///|
/// Proof-side classifier spec for `KernelEvent::is_terminal`.
///
/// Terminal means exactly one of the three terminal constructors
/// (RunCompleted / RunFailed / RunCancelled); every other event — including
/// the quiescent `RunSuspended` and the never-state-changing `InputRejected`
/// — is non-terminal. The predicate matches constructor tags only (bare
/// constructor names: the proof frontend rejects `..` rest patterns and
/// `label~` patterns, and labeled constructors take no positional arguments
/// in `.mbtp`), so payload types (String / Json / arrays) never enter the
/// logic body.

///|
/// Spec of `KernelEvent::is_terminal`: true iff the event is one of the three
/// terminal constructors; false for all run-lifecycle, model, tool, budget,
/// suspension and rejection events.
predicate is_terminal_event(e : KernelEvent) {
  match e {
    RunCompleted => true
    RunFailed => true
    RunCancelled => true
    _ => false
  }
}
